{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"summary\":\"The approach is broadly aligned, but the acceptance contract does not deterministically enforce its central stdout requirement and several deterministic stdout expectations are inconsistent with their commands.\",\"findings\":[{\"id\":\"stdout-outcome-only-not-enforced\",\"severity\":\"blocking\",\"summary\":\"The text-mode acceptance check permits arbitrary non-log output on stdout.\",\"detail\":\"The request and observable behaviour `text-stdout-outcome-only` require stdout to contain the rendered outcome and nothing else. However, the planned unit test and deterministic command only reject lines that look like JSON objects with a `\\\"level\\\"` key and confirm that the refusal text is present. An implementation could print diagnostics, warnings, or non-JSON log text to stdout and still pass. The test must compare stdout exactly with the expected rendered outcome, as the JSON-mode criterion already does.\",\"sections\":[\"Request — Objective\",\"Request — What should happen 3\",\"Plan — Proposed changes 3\",\"Acceptance contract — observable_behaviour.text-stdout-outcome-only\",\"Acceptance contract — deterministic.text-mode-stdout-carries-no-log-record\"]},{\"id\":\"deterministic-stdout-regexes-are\" ,\"severity\":\"blocking\",\"summary\":\"Several deterministic commands cannot satisfy their declared exact stdout match under ordinary regex semantics.\",\"detail\":\"The L01 and VC-POC-13 commands print every confidence line before their success marker; the no-grade command prints the blocks; and the text-mode command prints the rendered outcome. Their `expect.stdout_matches` values are nevertheless anchored as if the marker were the entire stdout, for example `^L01-BLOCK-OK$` and `^TEXT-STDOUT-OK$`. Unless the acceptance runner applies undocumented multiline line-search semantics, these checks fail after a correct implementation. The commands should suppress preceding diagnostic output or the expectations should explicitly match the complete output using defined matcher semantics.\",\"sections\":[\"Acceptance contract — deterministic.l01-block-shows-stated-grade\",\"Acceptance contract — deterministic.vc-poc-13-block-shows-component-grades\",\"Acceptance contract — deterministic.no-stated-grade-shows-ratings-only\",\"Acceptance contract — deterministic.text-mode-stdout-carries-no-log-record\"]}]}"}}
